{
  "_comment": "DragonMineZ voxel hair, recovered from com.dragonminez.common.hair (CustomHair/HairStrand/CustomHair$HairFace) with javap. A style is a list of strand GROUPS; scripts/entity/HairBuilder.gd expands each group into strands and each strand into a chain of cubes. Coordinates are head-local model units: the head cube spans x[-4,4] y[0,8] z[-4,4] with y=0 at the head pivot. Base slots per face: FRONT 1 row x 4 cols, BACK/LEFT/RIGHT/TOP 4 rows x 4 cols; col offsets [-3,-1,1,3], row drop [0,-1.5,-3,-4.5]. Base rotations: FRONT -90x, BACK +90x, LEFT +90z, RIGHT -90z, TOP none, so a strand always grows away from the skull. `rot` is added on top of that base, so on FRONT a POSITIVE x sweeps the strand up and forward and a negative one drops it into a fringe; on BACK it is the other way round; on TOP a positive x leans the spikes backwards; on LEFT a negative z sweeps up (mirrored on RIGHT).",
